# What must never reach the build context.
#
# `.env*` is the one that matters. `next build` reads .env.local if it finds
# one, and anything NEXT_PUBLIC_ in there is compiled into the client bundle —
# so a developer's local control plane, or worse a local credential, would ship
# inside the image. The deploy script passes what the build needs explicitly.
.env
.env.*

# Rebuilt inside the image, and copying a host build in would defeat the
# lockfile install and drag macOS-native binaries onto a linux base.
node_modules
.next
*.tsbuildinfo

.git
.gitignore
.DS_Store
npm-debug.log*

# Documentation and editor instructions have no bearing on the build.
README.md
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md
